{
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "title",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "# Mini-AES & Substitution-Permutation Network (SPN) Flow\n**Block Size**: 16 bits (4 nibbles $s_0, s_1, s_2, s_3$ arranged as a $2 \\times 2$ state matrix over $GF(2^4)$)\n**Core Architecture**: **Key Mixing** ($\\oplus$) $\\rightarrow$ **Substitution / S-Box** (Confusion) $\\rightarrow$ **Permutation / ShiftRow & MixColumn** (Diffusion)",
      "x": -450,
      "y": -320,
      "width": 1160,
      "height": 150,
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "k0_xor",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "### Round 0: Pre-Whitening (`AddRoundKey`)\n```cpp\nstate ^= K0; // 0x9C63 ^ 0xC3F0 = 0x5F93\n```\n- Mixes master key $K_0$ before the first S-Box\n- Without pre-whitening, the first S-Box layer has no secret key material!",
      "x": -350,
      "y": -120,
      "width": 660,
      "height": 150,
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "r1_sub",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "### Step 1: NibbleSub / S-Box ($\\gamma$)\n```cpp\ns[i] = SBOX[s[i]]; // 0x5F93 -> 0xF7A1\n```\n- **Confusion Layer**: Non-linear 4-bit lookup table\n- Destroys linearity over $GF(2)$ so ciphertext cannot be solved as a system of linear equations",
      "x": -350,
      "y": 80,
      "width": 660,
      "height": 170,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "r1_shift",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "### Step 2: ShiftRow / Wire Permutation ($\\pi$)\n```cpp\nswap(s[1], s[3]); // 0xF7A1 -> 0xF1A7\n```\n- **Inter-Column Diffusion**: Moves nibble $s_1$ into Column 1 and $s_3$ into Column 0\n- In classic SPN (`04_spn_cipher.cpp`), a 16-bit wire transpose (`P_BOX`) routes 1 bit from each S-Box to every next-round S-Box",
      "x": -350,
      "y": 300,
      "width": 660,
      "height": 180,
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "r1_mix",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "### Step 3: MixColumn in $GF(2^4)$ ($\\theta$)\n```cpp\n// Multiply each column by MDS matrix [3 2; 2 3] mod (x^4 + x + 1)\n// 0xF1A7 -> 0x0E3E, then XOR K1 (0x30FF) -> 0x3EC1\n```\n- **Intra-Column Diffusion**: Mixes top and bottom nibbles of each column over $GF(2^4)$\n- Together with `ShiftRow`, a 1-nibble change affects **all 4 nibbles** in just 2 rounds!",
      "x": -350,
      "y": 530,
      "width": 660,
      "height": 180,
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "r2_final",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "### Final Round: NibbleSub $\\rightarrow$ ShiftRow $\\rightarrow$ AddRoundKey($K_2$)\n```cpp\n// 0x3EC1 -> NibbleSub(0x1054) -> ShiftRow(0x1450) ^ K2(0x6696) = 0x72C6\n```\n- **No `MixColumn` (or `P_BOX`) in the final round!**\n- Matches real AES-128/256: a final unkeyed linear layer adds no security and is omitted to make encryption/decryption symmetric.",
      "x": -350,
      "y": 760,
      "width": 660,
      "height": 180,
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "spn_vs_arx",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## Week 1 (ARX) vs Week 2 (SPN)\n\n| Feature | ChaCha20 (ARX) | Mini-AES (SPN) |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Confusion** | Addition mod $2^{32}$ (`+`) | 4-bit S-Box Lookup (`SBOX[x]`) |\n| **Diffusion** | Bit Rotation (`<<< 16,12,8,7`) | `ShiftRow` + `MixColumn` / `P_BOX` |\n| **Key Mixing** | Embedded in 512-bit state | Explicit `AddRoundKey` (`^= K_r`) |\n| **Decryption** | Identical to Encryption (Stream XOR) | Inverse rounds (`INV_SBOX`, reverse keys) |",
      "x": 380,
      "y": -120,
      "width": 480,
      "height": 420,
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "gf16_math",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "## Galois Field $GF(2^4)$ Math\n- Irreducible polynomial: $P(x) = x^4 + x + 1$ (`0b10011 = 0x13`)\n- Addition in $GF(2^4)$ is just bitwise XOR (`^`)\n- Multiplication shifts left and XORs `0x13` whenever bit 4 overflows\n- Because $\\begin{bmatrix} 3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3 \\end{bmatrix}^2 = \\begin{bmatrix} 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\end{bmatrix}$ in $GF(2^4)$, `MixColumn` is **self-inverting**!",
      "x": 380,
      "y": 350,
      "width": 480,
      "height": 360,
      "color": "1"
    }
  ],
